        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Caño Negro Wildlife Refuge"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_text:19733866b693022b",
      "field": "highlight.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6db4cd5fbd705d50aaa170e06f0134b3e24dfcad4b49982ad3863f972a477759",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Take a comfortable boat along the Río Frío. The river begins at Los Chiles, a small town near the Nicaraguan border, and runs through the wildlife refuge.\n\nFrom the water, you may spot cattle egrets, cormorants, howler monkeys, white-faced monkeys, three-toed sloths, caimans, lizards and turtles. The boat trip itself lasts about three hours."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:27591fa18c797316",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f865bb39576144e0f285da5e13b092fc424a8fa590d3c8f21d42467d261e1750",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "The calm Río Frío and birds along the green banks of Caño Negro, Costa Rica"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_hover:6016d6300e2ceff5",
      "field": "media.hover",
      "sourceTextSha256": "54630ce050e9ffcb323ba1fd457322949f80884fd7a030a7645394e54e23ee75",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Caño Negro, Costa Rica, where birds fly over a quiet river bordered by greenery"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_title:3346585652cc3cf1",
      "field": "highlight.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "35e0933794c53f76fa3f304d807347193813ee00099c61da5221a53728519ff4",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Río Celeste"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:highlight_text:01fd85831a395232",
      "field": "highlight.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "594ea2b4e1878afbee4c1a024d4f51ae713f61e29e2135e19ded8da77cfcfd7b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "The Río Celeste flows through Tenorio Volcano National Park. The route follows cloud forest trails to Los Teñideros and the waterfall. The river is known for its vivid turquoise water, and there are hot springs along its banks."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:856955a438021115",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "483e76f0261b01e9dcd757aa5ab9ba2b44a3e81b57f19fa0e0f23c920fb8873a",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "The Río Celeste waterfall drops into a turquoise pool in the forest of Tenorio Volcano National Park, Costa Rica"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_hover:b38b3788db33331e",
      "field": "media.hover",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f3d0a5d1f433a3bec398adb4a0528cd294901a7fdad527ffd457eb3d3abdc927",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "The Río Celeste in Costa Rica, with pale turquoise water, rocks and dense greenery"
    }
  ]
